-matched connector vs role occupant identity break is large and significant (n=96). Licensed comparison excludes organizers.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=96 matched pairs vs role; n=25 vs terminal; 908 player-seasons\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-PAP-028"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-PAP-033", "score": 0.088, "document": "# FAM:SF-PAP-033 | Study family SF-PAP-033: Split-half validation of travel x fit outcome ordering\n- observed_research_question: Split-half validation of travel x fit outcome ordering\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: Additive > irrelevant on destination embedded minutes and on-court net rating survives when travel OLS and medians are fit on a calibration half and scored on holdout.\n- observed_result: 500 splits; embedded-rate gap median=+0.116 [10-90% -0.033, +0.248] P(>0)=0.838; net-rtg gap median=+2.926 [+0.541, +5.072] P(>0)=0.960; corr(travel forecast, net rtg) median=+0.178 P(>0)=0.976; corr(delta, net) median=+ [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: additive>irrelevant on net rating in 96% of holdout splits; minutes gap positive in 84%\n- observed_sample_and_power: n~198 movers, 500 splits, half~99\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPM-039\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-PAP-032\n- observed_verdict: supported"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-052", "score": 0.079, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-052 | Study family SF-APPA-052: CUT feasibility cap: BEST-AVOID gap without CUT-heavy games\n- observed_research_question: CUT feasibility cap: BEST-AVOID gap without CUT-heavy games\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: The BEST vs AVOID gap is inflated by games where CUT exceeds 15% of H2 mix.\n- observed_result: All games BEST 1.473 vs AVOID 0.853 gap +0.620 MW p=0.0000 Spearman -0.316 n=2,544. CUT<=15%: +0.625 n=2,508. CUT>15%: +0.163 n.s. n=36. Only 4/272 games had CUT>15%.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:BASE_RATE\n- observed_failure_evidence: Removing the 4 CUT-heavy games slightly strengthens the gap (+0.620 to +0.625).\n- observed_sample_and_power: 2,544 rows; 272 games\n- auto_validation_status: same_pipeline_validation; evidence: APPA-052: 'tale relative to n-gated +0.375 / best-vs-continue +0.445). robustness direction still holds on this csv. 2,544 rows; 272 game'\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF32\n- observed_verdict: supported\n- auto_confidence: high (1.0)"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{"action": "final", "output": {
  "research_concepts": [
    "cut-heavy shaper",
    "drive-heavy shaper",
    "role portability / travel",
    "offensive play-type share (CUT vs DRIVE)",
    "structural role classification (shaper)",
    "mover outcome metrics (embedded minutes, net rating)",
    "fit quadrant (additive vs irrelevant)"
